<title>ITALY: S&amp;P says Italy 1997 budget doesn't change its view.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P says Italy 1997 budget doesn't change its view.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's planned 62.5 trillion lire budget for 1997 does not change Standard &amp; Poor's opinion on the country's debt ratings, Susan Witt, director of S&amp;P in Paris, said at a news conference in Milan.</p>
<p>She said the package was &quot;compatible with a slowly improving trend, a positive trend...but which is already discounted in Italy's current rating,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>&quot;It is not a budget which will change our opinion.&quot;</p>
<p>S&amp;P affirmed Italy's AA foreign currency and AAA local currency ratings after April's general elections which brought Prime Minister Romano Prodi's centre-left government to power.</p>
</text>
